{
  "name": "fjall",
  "description": "Fjall is a thread-safe, log-structured merge-tree (LSM-tree) embeddable storage engine implemented in Rust, offering a BTreeMap-like API for ordered key-value access. It supports multiple isolated partitions with cross-partition atomic semantics, serializable snapshot isolation (SSI), and integrated compression via LZ4 or Zlib. The architecture optimizes for high-throughput writes and efficient range queries through tiered compaction and optional key-value separation for large-scale blob workloads.",
